1. Create a new folder for your extension and initialize it with a `package.json` file.

2. Install the necessary dependencies (Chrome Web Store SDK, Amazon Marketplace APIs, etc.) using npm or yarn:

```sh
npm install @google-cloud/firestore @google-cloud/firestore-node
npm install @google-cloud/storage
npm install @google-auth/client-service-account
npm install @aws-amplify/ui @aws-amplify/authentication
```

3. Create a new `manifest.json` file in your extension folder to define your extension's information, manifest version, and permissions:

```json
{
  "manifest_version": 2,
  "name": "Amazon Price Checker",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "description": "Check the price of Amazon items based on users' gender, apparent income class, and ethnicity.",
  "permissions": [
    "storage",
    "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/firebase-admin"
  ],
  "background": {
    "scripts": ["background.js"]
  },
  "content_scripts": []
}
```

